WEBVTT

00:00:00.594 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.763 --> 00:00:06.510
In this lesson, we do the preparation before lash extensions, step by step:

00:00:06.699 --> 00:00:10.350
from the moment the client walks in, to the moment the tool tray is ready.

00:00:10.698 --> 00:00:13.310
You learned how to apply the lashes in the classic lesson.

00:00:13.488 --> 00:00:16.270
Today, we stop just before the first lash.

00:00:16.947 --> 00:00:17.642
Step one:

00:00:17.965 --> 00:00:19.482
welcome and consultation.

00:00:20.076 --> 00:00:23.482
Wash your hands, and seat the client while her eyes are still open.

00:00:23.824 --> 00:00:27.162
Give her the consultation form, on paper or on a tablet.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:33.537
Ask about allergies, earlier reactions to lash glue or lash tint, eye conditions,

00:00:33.487 --> 00:00:34.922
recent eye surgery,

00:00:34.953 --> 00:00:38.602
contact lenses, medication, and whether she is pregnant.

00:00:39.108 --> 00:00:40.442
Ask what look she wants.

00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:43.002
Then let her read it all back, and agree.

00:00:43.681 --> 00:00:44.452
Step two:

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.852
look at the client's eyes in good light.

00:00:47.173 --> 00:00:49.892
Even light, the client sitting up and looking upward.

00:00:50.395 --> 00:00:55.332
Look for red or watery eyes, a stye, a swollen or crusty lash line.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.572
Look at her natural lashes too:

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:03.652
thick or sparse, strong or weak, any broken lashes, any patches of lash loss.

00:01:04.138 --> 00:01:08.532
If anything looks wrong, stop, as in the lesson on when not to do a service.

00:01:09.062 --> 00:01:11.741
Before you start, tell the client a few things.

00:01:12.115 --> 00:01:15.535
The appointment can last one to two hours, lying still,

00:01:15.485 --> 00:01:17.741
with her eyes closed the whole time.

00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:23.026
If her eyes sting, feel gritty, or she needs a break, she raises her hand,

00:01:22.976 --> 00:01:24.781
and does not open her eyes.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.581
And she should use the bathroom before lying down.

00:01:27.993 --> 00:01:32.192
When the client knows in advance, she feels calmer, lies stiller,

00:01:32.142 --> 00:01:33.661
and her eyes move less.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:35.116
Step three:

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:37.596
the patch test, for a first time client.

00:01:38.105 --> 00:01:40.556
Follow the glue maker's instructions exactly.

00:01:40.904 --> 00:01:44.476
It is usually done 24 to 48 hours before the appointment.

00:01:44.985 --> 00:01:48.289
The common way is to attach a few lashes at the outer corner,

00:01:48.239 --> 00:01:49.996
with the very glue you will use.

00:01:50.341 --> 00:01:54.556
Or put a tiny dot of glue near the lash line, as the maker instructs.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:55.996
Then tell the client:

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:00.832
at home, watch for redness, itching or swelling, and if there is any,

00:02:00.782 --> 00:02:01.836
call the salon.

00:02:02.213 --> 00:02:06.076
Write the test date, the glue, and the result in the client's profile.

00:02:06.582 --> 00:02:09.697
For a client who was tested before, open the profile,

00:02:09.647 --> 00:02:12.876
check the test date and the result, then ask her again:

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.276
since then, have your eyes been all right?

00:02:15.937 --> 00:02:16.734
Step four:

00:02:16.988 --> 00:02:18.494
prepare the bed and the lamp.

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:22.321
Wipe the bed with a disinfectant wipe, lay a fresh cover,

00:02:22.271 --> 00:02:24.174
and put on a new headrest liner.

00:02:24.442 --> 00:02:28.861
A neck pillow, a light blanket, and a lamp that lights the eye area evenly,

00:02:28.811 --> 00:02:31.134
without glaring straight into her face.

00:02:31.476 --> 00:02:35.584
Phone on silent, soft music, a comfortable room temperature,

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:37.614
so the client can truly relax.

00:02:37.863 --> 00:02:40.254
Wash your hands, then put on new gloves.

00:02:40.836 --> 00:02:41.714
Step five:

00:02:41.962 --> 00:02:45.554
the client takes out her contact lenses, and you remove her eye makeup.

00:02:45.964 --> 00:02:47.716
Contact lenses come out first,

00:02:47.666 --> 00:02:51.234
because glue fumes and liquids can get trapped under the lens.

00:02:51.611 --> 00:02:56.274
All eye makeup, mascara and creams come off with an oil free makeup remover.

00:02:56.607 --> 00:03:00.114
If any oil is left on the lashes, the glue will not hold well.

00:03:00.792 --> 00:03:01.732
Step six:

00:03:01.966 --> 00:03:03.172
cleanse the lashes.

00:03:03.739 --> 00:03:05.972
The client lies down with her eyes closed.

00:03:06.348 --> 00:03:10.932
With lash cleanser and a soft brush, brush gently from the base to the tips.

00:03:11.281 --> 00:03:14.769
Then rinse with clean water, flowing gently from the top down,

00:03:14.719 --> 00:03:16.932
with a tissue held at the outer corner.

00:03:17.438 --> 00:03:22.212
After that, dry them thoroughly with a small fan, held at a distance from the face.

00:03:22.392 --> 00:03:26.292
The lashes must be completely dry, or the glue will not bond well.

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:27.728
Step seven:

00:03:27.982 --> 00:03:29.408
the under eye pads.

00:03:29.974 --> 00:03:32.368
This is the step most often done carelessly.

00:03:32.637 --> 00:03:35.134
The pad must fully cover the lower lashes,

00:03:35.084 --> 00:03:38.048
with its top edge right under the lower lash line.

00:03:38.396 --> 00:03:42.448
But it must not touch the waterline, and must not touch the eye itself.

00:03:42.794 --> 00:03:47.090
If it touches the waterline, the client will feel scratchiness and stinging,

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.208
her eyes will water,

00:03:48.398 --> 00:03:50.208
and they will be red after the appointment.

00:03:50.616 --> 00:03:51.328
A small tip:

00:03:51.509 --> 00:03:55.802
ask the client to open her eyes slightly and look up while you place the pad,

00:03:55.752 --> 00:03:58.448
so its edge tucks neatly under the lower lashes,

00:03:58.715 --> 00:04:00.128
then let her close her eyes.

00:04:00.426 --> 00:04:03.488
When it is on, ask the client whether it feels scratchy.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.808
If it does, adjust it right away.

00:04:06.077 --> 00:04:08.368
Never let her put up with it for the whole appointment.

00:04:09.102 --> 00:04:10.535
A very common mistake:

00:04:10.759 --> 00:04:13.079
placing the pad too low, or crooked,

00:04:13.029 --> 00:04:16.295
so a few lower lashes poke out at the outer corner.

00:04:16.877 --> 00:04:21.015
When you apply the lashes, those lower lashes get glued to the upper ones.

00:04:21.353 --> 00:04:25.095
When the client opens her eyes, they pull, and it really hurts.

00:04:25.435 --> 00:04:28.541
So once the pad is on, check carefully along its edge,

00:04:28.491 --> 00:04:30.295
especially at the outer corner.

00:04:30.859 --> 00:04:31.579
Step eight:

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:33.019
tape, when needed.

00:04:33.444 --> 00:04:38.029
If any lower lashes still poke out, add a small piece of medical paper tape,

00:04:37.979 --> 00:04:39.819
only on the pad and the cheek,

00:04:39.849 --> 00:04:40.859
never on the eye.

00:04:41.208 --> 00:04:42.197
For hooded eyes,

00:04:42.147 --> 00:04:46.539
many technicians use a small piece of tape to gently lift the eyelid skin,

00:04:46.729 --> 00:04:48.779
so the lash line is clearly visible.

00:04:49.204 --> 00:04:52.299
Apply it gently, and ask the client whether it feels tight.

00:04:52.926 --> 00:04:53.739
Step nine:

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:58.059
brush the lashes, then apply primer, if the glue maker recommends it.

00:04:58.611 --> 00:05:01.979
Primer removes the remaining oils, so the glue bonds better.

00:05:02.485 --> 00:05:04.163
With a disposable micro brush,

00:05:04.113 --> 00:05:07.419
sweep it lightly over the middle and the tips of the lashes,

00:05:07.448 --> 00:05:09.739
well away from the base and the eyelid skin.

00:05:10.248 --> 00:05:13.179
Then brush the lashes again, so they separate evenly.

00:05:13.841 --> 00:05:14.617
Step ten:

00:05:14.856 --> 00:05:16.057
the tool tray is ready.

00:05:16.402 --> 00:05:21.028
Lash trays according to the map, a jade stone with a fresh drop of glue,

00:05:20.978 --> 00:05:22.617
two disinfected tweezers,

00:05:22.826 --> 00:05:25.657
a lash wand, and disposable micro brushes.

00:05:26.006 --> 00:05:27.657
Cap the glue bottle straight away.

00:05:28.086 --> 00:05:31.817
Check the room humidity and temperature again, against the glue maker's range.

00:05:32.166 --> 00:05:33.817
And one last question for the client:

00:05:34.373 --> 00:05:37.257
is she comfortable lying like this, is her neck all right?

00:05:37.488 --> 00:05:38.617
Now you are ready.

00:05:38.791 --> 00:05:43.017
From the first lash onward, carry on as in the classic practice lesson.

00:05:43.668 --> 00:05:44.614
Remember the order:

00:05:44.795 --> 00:05:51.371
consultation, eye check, patch test, clean bed, lenses out, cleanse, pads,

00:05:51.321 --> 00:05:52.694
tape if needed,

00:05:52.881 --> 00:05:54.294
brush, tray ready.

00:05:54.686 --> 00:05:57.254
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
